  "description": "HIBYID crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H88 Dy4 N8 O20,1.63(C2 H3 N1),0.37(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.802-3.860 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.93-108.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(dbm)6(L)2(μ3-OH)2]·CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
